  "nl_text": "The rschema_0122 database is designed to manage conversations, customer interactions, and organization information. At its core, the database consists of six tables: conversation, message, inquiry, organization, security_base_record, and customer. The conversation table stores unique conversation IDs, customer IDs, creation and last update times, and a base ID that references the security_base_record table, which stores encrypted information and timestamps for each record. Each conversation is associated with a customer through the customer ID, and messages within a conversation are stored in the message table, which references the conversation ID. The inquiry table records customer inquiries, including the customer ID, inquiry category, content, status, creation, and end times, with a composite primary key of customer ID and creation time. The organization table contains information about organizations, including their IDs, names, phone numbers, avatars, locations, emails, descriptions, and homepage and image links. The customer table stores customer information, including IDs, names, contact details, and the organization they belong to, which is referenced by the organization ID. The database enforces referential integrity through foreign key constraints, ensuring that conversations are tied to customers and security base records, messages are tied to conversations, inquiries are tied to customers, and customers are tied to organizations.",
  "gold_question": "The Customer Relationship Management (CRM) or Customer Service system is used to manage customer inquiries, conversation records, and organization information. Its main features include:\n1.Conversation Management: Records basic information about each conversation, including Conversation ID, Customer ID, Organization ID, Creation Time, Last Update Time, and baseId.\n2.Inquiry Management: Records customer inquiry information, including the status (open, closed, draft), category, content, creation time, and end time of the inquiry.\n3.Organization Information Management: Records the basic information of organizations, such as phone number, avatar, location, email, description, homepage link, and image link. Supports detailed management and updating of organization information, ensuring each organization has a unique phone number and avatar. Customers belong to specific organizations.\n4.Data Security: Ensures each conversation is linked to a secure base record, including baseId, encrypted information, creation time, and update time to enhance system security.\nEach customer has a unique Customer ID, name, and contact information.\nEach inquiry may involve multiple customers.\nEach conversation may involve multiple customers and multiple organizations.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0122.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0122\nCREATE TABLE `conversation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `security_base_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`security_base_record_id`) REFERENCES `security_base_record` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversation` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inquiry` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `created_at`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `organization` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `homepage` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `security_base_record` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `encrypted_data` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `organization_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`organization_id`) REFERENCES `organization` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
